+---
+type: adr
+status: stable
+entities: [Comment, CommentReport, Post]
+related:
+  - app/Http/Controllers/CommentController.ts
+  - app/Http/Controllers/PostController.ts
+  - app/Http/Resources/CommentResource.ts
+  - app/Policies/CommentPolicy.ts
+generated: { by: "claude-fable/5.1", at: 2026-09-25T05:15:30.656Z }
+---
+
+# Community moderation hides comments after three reports
+
+## Context
+
+Readers can comment on posts, and the community has to keep that space
+clean without a moderator on call. Comments must not be something one bad
+actor can fill with spam, but nothing may be lost before a human can
+review it.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Any signed-in user may comment on any post and report any comment.
+  Reports live in `comment_reports`, one row per `(comment_id, user_id)`
+  (composite primary key), so repeating a report is a no-op and never
+  counts twice. Reporting always answers 204.
+- A comment with reports from three or more distinct users
+  (`HIDE_REPORT_THRESHOLD` in the Comment model) is left out of the post
+  page for everyone, its author and the post's author included. The row
+  stays in `comments` for later review; a review screen is out of scope.
+- Deleting is a hard delete, allowed only to the comment's author and the
+  author of the post it is on (`CommentPolicy.delete`). Deleting a post
+  removes its comments and their reports explicitly in a transaction, not
+  by relying on `ON DELETE CASCADE`, which SQLite only enforces when
+  `foreign_keys` is on.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Spam disappears from the page as soon as three readers flag it, with no
+moderator involved, and nothing is destroyed by reports alone. Three
+colluding accounts can hide a legitimate comment until someone reviews the
+`comment_reports` table; that review tooling is a later decision.
